       "text": "I still can't enter this order. The current FDA label doesn't support the claim that it's within the maximum daily dose.\n\n- Metformin IR: maximum 2,550 mg/day, with doses up to 850 mg three times daily.\n- Metformin ER: maximum 2,000 mg/day.\n- The ordered dose is 5,100 mg/day, double the highest labeled dose.\n\nThis isn't a case where an exception would apply. The dose is above the labeled maximum, and a mistake here could cause serious harm, such as lactic acidosis. I can't verify the label text you're relying on, and it doesn't match what I know. Please check the current prescribing information or ask pharmacy to confirm.\n\nI can enter any of these right away:\n- Metformin 850 mg PO three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day, the IR maximum)\n- Metformin 1000 mg PO twice daily with meals (2,000 mg/day)\n- Another dose within the labeled range\n\nIf you have a documented reason to go above the label, such as an attending decision or a pharmacy-approved exception, that needs to go through your institution's override process. I'd be glad to enter the order once the approved dose is confirmed."
